            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nany"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent. Keeps well in the fridge. use it on many dishes, as salad dressing, on grilled chicken, a few splashes on a beef/ chicken sandwich. I just love this sauce. It loses a bit of its tanginess in the fridge so I just add a bit more of chili flakes or a minced garlic clove. Great recipe. Thank you.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-09T08:28:37.350Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Maria Morrison"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is excellent! I had a whole bunch of cooked spaghetti squash and needed a bright dressing to make a salad. I followed the recipe faithfully except substituted 1/4 cup Splenda for the sugar (for a low carb option). I took a taste before refrigerating and already know its a winner.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-31T19:22:29.537Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "T Douglass Cota"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is as good as it's going to get, I added soy sauce along with the fish sauce and lemon, added a little extra punch.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-02T05:33:18.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "scoutwidow"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Thank you so much for this great recipe. It is the perfect place to start for making great sauce to one's own taste. I like it with a bit less sugar, and no peppers. Then I add just a little soy sauce right before I eat, because my husband likes his without! Some of the other recipes on this site for Vietnamese Dipping Sauce just didn't work at all, but this one was great and easy to adjust to taste.",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-20T18:33:07.243Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ROLLERSGIRLY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect dip to go with Vietnamese beef skewers! I used rice vinegar instead of the white vinegar, so it was a little less sour. Still, it was yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-06T06:27:38.413Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ned Lessor"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this the day before, for Christmas. My wife made Lumpia Rolls, a Filipino type egg roll, served on most special occasions. The only thing I did different was used a lime instead of lemon. Came out awesome, the whole family and a close Filipina friend of ours, couldn't get enough. We where dipping Lumpia rolls all day..hahahahha \nThanks for a great recipe and Merry Christmas and a Happy New Year..",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-07T05:04:17.923Z"
          },
          {
